Titre$Artificial Key to Arizona Earthstars (Geastraceae and Astraeus) 
com$ tiré de www.azfungi.org / 2009
1,0$a. Endoperidial body supported by several stalks, having multiple stomata; spores reticulate; exoperidium lustrous$Myriostoma coliforme
1,2$b. Endoperidial body sessile or supported by a single stalk, having a single stoma; spores not reticulate; exoperidium not lustrous
2,0$a. Gleba containing numerous thin or thick-walled paracapillitia, eucapillitia  lacking; spores echinate to verrucose; endoperidium reticulate, particularly on the  lower portion of the endoperidial body$Astraeus hygrometricus
2,3$b. Gleba containing numerous thick-walled eucapillitia; spores verrucose, but  not echinate; endoperidium not reticulate
3,4$a. Peristome fibrillose
3,18$b. Peristome plicate
4,5$a. Gasterocarp fornicate
4,6$b. Gasterocarp not fornicate
5,0$a. Peristome disc-shaped, distinctly delimited by a raised rim; endoperidium lacking pigmented protruding hyphae; gasterocarp of small to medium stature (less than 35 mm in height); spores 5.6-6.4 µm in diameter (including ornamentation)$Geastrum quadrifidum
5,0$b. Peristome not disc-shaped, nor distinctly delimited or only faintly so, lacking a rim; endoperidium densely covered with thick, pigmented protruding hyphae; gasterocarp of medium to large stature (greater than 35 mm in height); spores 4.8-5.6 µm in diameter (including ornamentation)$Geastrum fornicatum
6,7$a. Endoperidial body sessile
6,14$b. Endoperidial body stalked
7,9$a. Mycelial layer present (membranaceous or encrusted); rays sub to non-hygroscopic
7,8$b. Mycelial layer lacking; rays hygroscopic
8,0$a. Peristome distinctly delimited; spores 4.8-5.6 µm in diameter (including  ornamentation)$Geastrum corollinum
8,0$b. Peristome not distinctly delimited; spores 5.6-7.2 µm in diameter (including  ornamentation)$Geastrum floriforme
9,10$a. Peristome distinctly delimited
9,13$b. Peristome not distinctly delimited
10,0$a. Endoperidial body ringed by a pseudoparenchymatous collar; gasterocarp  saccate$Geastrum triplex
10,11$b. Endoperidial body not ringed by a pseudoparenchymatous collar; gasterocarp  saccate or not
11,0$a. Gasterocarp not saccate; peristome darker than endoperidial body, lacking a rim; mycelial layer heavily encrusted with debris or particles of soil or sand, not splitting radially along rays; spores 3.2-4.0 µm in diameter (including ornamentation)$Geastrum arenarium
11,12$b. Gasterocarp saccate; peristome concolorous with endoperidial body, distinctly rimmed; mycelial layer membranaceous, not encrusted with debris or only lightly so, often splitting radially along rays; spores 4.0-5.6 µm in diameter (including ornamentation)
12,0$a. Gasterocarp small to medium stature (less than 35 mm in width); spores 4.0-  4.8 µm in diameter (including ornamentation); spore mass light brown; tips of rays narrow$Geastrum lageniforme
12,0$b. Gasterocarp of medium to large stature (greater than 30 mm in width); spores  4.8-5.6 µm in diameter (including ornamentation); spore mass dark brown; tips of  rays narrow or truncate$Geastrum saccatum
13,0$a. Spores 3.2-4.0 µm in diameter (including ornamentation); gasterocarp of small to medium stature (less than 30 mm in height), often saccate; pseudoparenchymatous layer lacking reddish tints when fresh; fibrous layer papery to coriaceous$Geastrum fimbriatum
13,0$b. Spores 4.8-5.6 µm in diameter (including ornamentation); gasterocarp of medium to large stature (greater than 25 mm in height), never saccate; pseudoparenchymatous layer having reddish tints when fresh; fibrous layer coriaceous to rigid$Geastrum rufescens
14,0$b. Mycelial layer membranaceous, not encrusted with debris or only lightly so;  gasterocarp often pseudofornicate$Geastrum smardae
14,15$a. Mycelial layer lacking or not membranaceous, if present then heavily  encrusted with debris; gasterocarp never pseudofornicate
15,16$a. Peristome distinctly delimited
15,17$b. Peristome not distinctly delimited
16,0$a. Endoperidial body having a dense pruinose layer of crystalline matter; spores  4.8-6.4 µm in diameter; peristome distinctly delimited but not ringed by a pale  zone; gasterocarp of small to medium stature (less than 25 mm in height)$Geastrum minimum
16,0$b. Endoperidial body not having a dense pruinose layer of crystalline matter, or  only finely so; spores 5.6-6.4 µm in diameter; peristome distinctly delimited and  often ringed by a pale zone; gasterocarp of medium to large stature (greater than  20 mm in height)$Geastrum coronatum
17,0$a. Endoperidium covered with dark, persistent, coarse, granular, irregular-shaped to spiny projections; pseudoparenchymatous layer not having reddish tints when fresh; spores 4.0-4.8 µm in diameter (including ornamentation)$Geastrum hieronymi
17,0$b. Endoperidium not covered with dark, persistent, coarse, granular, irregular-shaped to spiny projections; pseudoparenchymatous layer having reddish tints when fresh; spores 4.8-5.6 µm in diameter (including ornamentation)$Geastrum rufescens
18,19$a. Endoperidial body sessile
18,21$b. Endoperidial body stalked
19,0$a. Mycelial layer lacking; rays hygroscopic; endoperidium verrucose$Geastrum kotlabae
19,20$b. Mycelial layer present; rays sub- to non-hygroscopic; endoperidium not verrucose
20,0$a. Endoperidial body having a dense pruinose layer of crystalline matter when  fresh; endoperidium glabrous; rays not truncate or broken off at tips$Geastrum elegans
20,0$b. Endoperidial body not having a dense pruinose layer of crystalline matter  when fresh; endoperidium minutely furfuraceous (hyphal protrusions visible only  under magnification); rays often truncate or broken off at tips$Geastrum xerophilum
21,0$a. Exoperidium verrucose; rays hygroscopic, occasionally only weakly so; spores 6.4-8.0 µm in diameter (including ornamentation); fibrous layer coriaceous to rigid$Geastrum campestre
21,22$b. Exoperidium not verrucose; rays sub to non-hygroscopic; spores 4.8-6.4 µm in diameter (including ornamentation); fibrous layer coriaceous
22,0$a. Endoperidial body not having a pruinose layer of matted hyphal elements  and/or crystalline matter when fresh; rays often truncate or broken off at tips$Geastrum xerophilum
22,23$b. Endoperidial body having a pruinose layer of matted hyphal elements and/or  crystalline matter when fresh; rays not truncate or broken off at tips
23,0$a. Spores 5.6-6.4 µm in diameter (including ornamentation); apophysis not forming a ridged collar$Geastrum schmidelii
23,24$b. Spores 4.8-5.6 µm in diameter (including ornamentation); apophysis forming a ridged collar or not
24,0$a. Apophysis forming a ridged collar; peristome plicate, not delimited or only  faintly so, conical and coming to a point at apex; gleba reddish brown$Geastrum striatum
24,0$b. Apophysis not forming a ridged collar; peristome deeply plicate, distinctly  delimited and often recessed, applanate, often raised in central portion to a short,narrow point; gleba dark brown$Geastrum smithii
